      "settlementKey": "ceulrithan:Cindrau",
      "description": "Dr. Evran Watson is a disciplined Hobgoblin robotics chair who sees artificial bodies as tools, citizens, weapons, and theological problems depending on who is funding the meeting. He is fascinated by construct cognition, Wechselkind adaptation, relicborn memory vessels, and the moment a machine's purpose becomes a preference. Evran is more humane than some Directorate peers, but his curiosity still outruns his caution when a new mind begins answering back.",
      "settlementAndAncestryTexture": "Cindrau is a City in Ceulrithan, under Confessional State, with high danger, Partial forest, Beach and grass with water, Farming terrain. Local records favor Altruistic, Lawful, Cooperative, Honorable civic habits; common communities include Human, Halfling — Lightfoot Halfling, Halfling — Stout Halfling, Kender, Kithkin. Hobgoblin reads through the Hobgoblin entry of the race compendium, within Orcs, Goblins, and Goblinoid Kin, marked by Enkirael. Hobgoblins are disciplined goblinoids organized around military hierarchy and strategy. They value order, structure, and coordinated warfare above individual freedom. Table cues: Goblinoid, Darkvision, Fey Ancestry, Fey Gift; starting tendency Selfish - Lawful - Cooperative - Honorable.",
      "rumors": [
        "Evran records apologies to prototypes he officially claims cannot understand them.",
        "His lab has more spare names than spare bodies."
      ],
      "plotHooks": [
        "Evran asks the party to recover a missing construct before Justen Ayo classifies it as stolen property.",
        "A machine built by Evran refuses to leave him, claiming it knows what he erased from its first memory."
      ],
